13:NMF is an unsupervised machine learning method used to decompose matrices; it can be used for dimension reduction and extraction of features (1) and has been widely utilized across multiple fields in MRI data analysis (2), image analysis (3), and signal processing (4). Compared with principle component analysis, independent component analysis, and singular value decomposition, NMF  can  capture  robust  and  reliable  non-negative  underlying  structural  differences  in  high dimension data, and is well-suited for structural MRI to detect differences among individuals.
21:In our study, we used the multiplicative update method to obtained the factors and weights, which is the most commonly used method for solving the NMF problem. The package for NMF is available at https://github.com/smatmo/l0-sparse-NMF. NMF was first applied on the ABIDE\_II\_TD GM matrix, and it was decomposed to six factors and their corresponding weights (Fig.1 (b)). Then, the  non-negative  reconstruction  algorithm  was  used  to  reconstruct  the  ABIDE\_I\_ASD  and ABIDE\_I\_TD GM matrices (Figs.1(c) and 1(d), respectively). The strategy iteratively updates the H matrix, while keeping the W matrix obtained from the ABIDE\_II\_TD GM matrix decomposition fixed. A two-sample t -test was utilized to examine group differences in the weights obtained from the
53:The  multiplicative  update  method  (https://github.com/smatmo/l0-sparse-NMF)  was  used  to solve the NMF problem and estimate the subject loading matrix (11). The difference between NMF and BR-NMF is that BR-NMF iteratively updates the H matrix, while keeping the W matrix obtained from the ABIDE\_II\_TD GM matrix decomposition fixed, and does not stop until the reconstruction error is almost unchanged compared with the previous iteration.
128:In ABIDE\_I\_TD participants, we found that all of the weights were associated positively with FIQ.  In  previous  studies,  FSIQ  has  been  shown  to  correlate  positively  with  GM  volume  in  left superior temporal gyrus, bilateral supramarginal gyrus, and left fusiform gyrus in adults and with GM volume in frontal, parietal, and cerebellar regions in children (20-22). In order to exclude the effects of covariates on weights, we used the generalized linear model method to regress out age, gender, handedness, FSIQ, and sites when comparing the difference of weights and deviations between ASD and TD.
